"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[7575],{97575:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"gajd-2-kreditka","title":"Guide 2. A credit card without interest: For people with no debts and a cushion","sourceFingerprint":"e892e3fa2b3f145cd3e359fb14f3dd1cc761e41099a05214669eba8573d35a40","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"## A credit card without interest"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"For people with no debts and a cushion"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"A credit card can be a free tool: pay everyday purchases with it and repay the entire balance before grace ends. Use the bank’s money without interest while your own stays in savings earning interest."},{"id":"b004","markdown":"This is an advanced guide. Without confidence and discipline, the card becomes a loan at 50% annually, and one late payment consumes a year’s benefit. Start only after the first step."},{"id":"b005","markdown":"### Step 1: Check whether it suits you at all"},{"id":"b006","markdown":"Every condition must hold at once:"},{"id":"b007","markdown":"No expensive debts; lessons 4 and 5."},{"id":"b008","markdown":"- A cushion of at least 3 months is complete; lesson 6."},{"id":"b009","markdown":"- You have never paid card interest or missed a payment."},{"id":"b010","markdown":"- You know exactly how much you spend monthly; lesson 2."},{"id":"b011","markdown":"If even one does not apply, stop here. That is a valid choice and you lose nothing important."},{"id":"b012","markdown":"### Step 2: Calculate the actual benefit"},{"id":"b013","markdown":"Use monthly card-eligible spending and your savings-account rate. On average, each purchase leaves your money earning for roughly 40 extra days. For example, spending 60 000 RUB monthly with savings at 13%: 720 000 RUB yearly \xd7 40/365 \xd7 13% ≈ 10 000 RUB yearly, plus cashback if available. If the result is under a couple of thousand annually, it may not justify the effort."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"### Step 3: Choose a card"},{"id":"b015","markdown":"Check 4 tariff details:"},{"id":"b016","markdown":"The grace period: how many days and whether counted from purchase or statement-period start."},{"id":"b017","markdown":"- Servicing: free, or free under a clear condition."},{"id":"b018","markdown":"- Operations cancelling grace: usually cash withdrawals and transfers, sometimes particular purchase categories."},{"id":"b019","markdown":"- Cashback: whether available and on what.\\nImportant: one credit card is enough. Several with different due dates sharply increase mistake risk."},{"id":"b020","markdown":"### Step 4: Disable unnecessary extras"},{"id":"b021","markdown":"Immediately after opening, check the app for insurance, paid notifications and other paid services. Banks often enable these by default. Insurance sold when opening can be cancelled and refunded within 30 days."},{"id":"b022","markdown":"### Step 5: Automate full repayment and a reminder"},{"id":"b023","markdown":"If possible, automate repayment of the full balance from your account before grace ends. Not the minimum: the entire balance. Add a calendar reminder 3–5 days before expiry. Important: even a day late can trigger full-rate interest for the whole period since purchases."},{"id":"b024","markdown":"### Step 6: Use it only for purchases"},{"id":"b025","markdown":"Pay ordinary shop and online purchases. Do not withdraw cash or transfer from the card: these nearly always cancel grace and incur fees. One safety rule applies: card debt must always be smaller than the money currently available in your account."},{"id":"b026","markdown":"### Step 7: Reconcile monthly"},{"id":"b027","markdown":"When the statement arrives, compare spending with the period before card use.\\nIn an MIT experiment by Drazen Prelec and Duncan Simester (2001), participants were willing to pay more than twice as much for basketball tickets using a credit card rather than cash. If switching raises your spending, the benefit disappears; return to a debit card."},{"id":"b028","markdown":"### Outcome"},{"id":"b029","markdown":"If correctly arranged, you:"},{"id":"b030","markdown":"- Pay purchases using bank money without charge."},{"id":"b031","markdown":"- Keep your money earning in savings for an extra month to month-and-a-half."},{"id":"b032","markdown":"- Receive cashback where the card offers it."},{"id":"b033","markdown":"- Pay the bank no interest."},{"id":"b034","markdown":"At the first interest payment or noticeable spending increase, stop and return to a debit card."}],"terms":[],"quizzes":[],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);